From: Raspberry Pi camera firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] avutil/drm: let the device callback own failure cleanup

Pi's rpi_29 patch registers drm_device_free before opening the device. When
drmGetVersion fails, av_hwdevice_ctx_create unreferences the device context
and invokes that callback. Closing the descriptor here as well can close
an unrelated descriptor reused by another thread between the two calls.
Leave the single close to the already registered cleanup callback.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_drm.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_drm.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_drm.c
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_drm.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_drm.c
@@ -135,7 +135,6 @@ static int drm_device_create(AVHWDeviceContext *hwdev, const char *device,
     if (!version) {
         av_log(hwdev, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Failed to get version information "
                "from %s: probably not a DRM device?\n", device);
-        close(hwctx->fd);
         return AVERROR(EINVAL);
     }
 
